      "retrieved": "2026-10-12",
      "revision": 1314503336,
      "text": "Avena abyssinica, also known as the Ethiopian oat and \"Ajja\" by Ethiopians, is a member of the family Poaceae. This grain has long been used in Ethiopia and is well adapted to the high elevations and other conditions there. Still a traditional food plant in Africa, this little-known grain has potential to improve nutrition, boost food security, foster rural development and support sustainable landcare."
